# P13-006: pushdown cascade + projection-driven genotypes

Make a `WHERE` on `c.genotypes` **skip whole cells** (not just row groups inside already-opened
cells), and make projecting a derived column (`het`, `missing`, `n_alt`, …) avoid a full genotype
decode. This is the performance layer P13-003 deferred, with **predicate pushdown into the catalog
prune** as the core (Teague's original thrust).

Supersedes the "P13-004" placeholder that earlier docs used for cascade + projection — this is that
work, plus pushdown. Depends on: P13-003 (ATTACH, merged #82) and P13-005 (ATTACH all kinds). The
writer path is now **P13-007** (penciled, separate).

